## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design real-time blind source separation systems for mobile platforms with dynamic geometry and environmental noise challenges, emphasizing adaptive signal processing, cross-bin coherence, and multimodal self-supervised learning approaches.

## Key Concepts

- Geometry-aware whitening with adaptive tracking
- Online ICA versus joint diagonalization strategies
- Dynamic demixer scaling and computational cadence
- Cross-bin permutation alignment using envelope analysis
- Video-driven self-supervised permutation stabilization

## Code Example

```javascript
// Geometry-aware online whitening with forgetting factor
function geometryAwareWhitening(micSignals, forgettingFactor = 0.95) {
  const covariance = updateCovariance(micSignals, forgettingFactor);
  const whiteningMatrix = computeWhiteningMatrix(covariance);
  return applyWhitening(micSignals, whiteningMatrix);
}

// Adaptive switching between per-bin ICA and joint diagonalization
function selectICAStrategy(signalQuality, frequencyBins) {
  if (signalQuality > THRESHOLD_HIGH) {
    return 'jointDiagonalization';
  } else if (signalQuality > THRESHOLD_LOW) {
    return 'perBinICA';
  }
  return 'hybridApproach';
}

// Cross-bin permutation alignment using envelope correlation
function alignPermutations(separatedSources, sampleRate) {
  const envelopes = computeEnvelopes(separatedSources);
  const correlationMatrix = computeEnvelopeCorrelation(envelopes);
  return resolvePermutationAmbiguity(correlationMatrix);
}

// Self-supervised loss using synchronized video
function videoGuidedLoss(audioSources, videoFeatures) {
  const audioVisualCorrelation = computeCrossModalCorrelation(audioSources, videoFeatures);
  return -audioVisualCorrelation.mean(); // Minimize negative correlation
}
```

